\begin{abstract}
The Astromorphic Simulation Engine (ASE-X) is a hierarchical,
multi-physics computational architecture designed to integrate
high-resolution observational data ingestion, differentiable
magnetohydrodynamics (MHD) and N-body solvers, neural operator
unknowns mapping, and simulation-based inference (SBI) into a
single sovereign substrate. ASE-X formalizes the coupling between
astrophysical data, governing PDEs, anomaly residual learning,
and posterior estimation using normalizing flows. This paper
presents the mathematical structure, execution workflow, and
stress-test invariants of ASE-X.
\end{abstract}

